    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1010">

                <pb facs="1258" n="1240" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24523/8–2746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cooper</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-27T18:00:00-04:00">August 27, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>754. War Dept advises court martial at Talara deferred accordance your
                    instructions. Presume this action taken as consequence of ForMin’s note
                    insisting on Peruvian jurisdiction. Dept would <pb facs="1259" n="1241"
                        xml:id="pg1241"/> appreciate your views as to why court martial should be
                    deferred pending understanding Peruvian Govt on question jurisdiction. If
                    military trial held should deal with all seven soldiers named by ForMin and none
                    should be allowed leave Perú pending adjudication.</p>
                <p>Base Commander Talara complains Lima authorities not responding his requests make
                    available necessary Peruvian witnesses.</p>
                <p>Cable reply requested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
